    description: "[REVIEW 2026-11-01, PARTLY-STALE] Reviewed 2026-11-01 on dev 100b6fbb6e. fdd99a9eae (INV-vokut, 2026-09-28) fixed the fully qualified form: `scala.sys.process.Process(c).!` now emits scala:scala.sys.process.Process:0-0:Process and classifies subprocess (plus a deliberate simultaneous fs_write row). `sys.process.Process(\"git ...\").!!` still emits scala:external:0-0:Process with call_construct=method and reaches no boundary. Only the sys-rooted half remains. (Original text below; the review entry in the thread has the evidence.)\n\nFOUND 2026-09-24 while measuring WI-narij.\n\nA fully qualified call loses its qualifier:\n- `scala.sys.process.Process(c).!` and `sys.process.Process(c).!` are emitted as `scala:external:0-0:Process`, stamped call_construct=method.\n- gate_named_entry never matches a method-stamped call with no context, so neither form classifies after WI-narij either.\nFixture: /tmp scratch; the three lines above reproduce it.\n\nCorpus: spark core/.../api/r/BaseRRunner.scala:282 and scala3 project/RepublishPlugin.scala:393 (`sys.process.Process(\"git rev-parse HEAD\").!!`). Those are 2 edges on 11 repos, so the volume is small.\n\nASKED: the scala analyzer writes a dotted qualifier into the module slot, as java.py does for `java.lang.System.getenv`. Measure what else changes; every qualified call is affected, not only Process."  # 5bcd
